From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett Lamy <blamy@Bretts-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:51:04 -0500
Subject: Add Replay's debugger to the browser process's Node

The process binding's record/replay methods, process.recordreplay, and the
JS which handles the debugger's commands, from Replay's Node. That fork also
annotates Node's threads and its GC callbacks so that they're the same when
replaying, and loads the driver at startup. An Electron browser process needs
none of that: it attaches before anything runs, its recorded threads run one
at a time, and V8 does the same things on both sides.

